# The corpus and the fixtures must arrive byte for byte identical on every
# platform, because ParityTest hashes them.
#
# Git's default autocrlf on Windows rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout. For these
# files that changes the bytes, which changes the SHA-256, which fails the
# manifest check before a single ranking is compared - and it would fail only
# on Windows clones, which is the worst kind of failure to debug.
#
# The chunk offsets depend on this too: a CRLF corpus shifts every offset after
# the first line break, so every chunk id would differ from the exported ones.

*.txt   text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf

# Java sources and the build file do not affect any hash, but keeping the whole
# tree LF avoids a diff that is nothing but line endings.
*.java  text eol=lf
*.xml   text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
